### Project Type Detection (Run This First)

**Single Source of Truth:** If `.jules/pm/project-classification.md` exists, use it and skip keyword detection. Fallback to keyword detection only if classification is missing.

```bash
# Detect project type before summary
PROJECT_TYPE="UNKNOWN"

# Check product vision
if [ -f ".jules/pm/product-vision.md" ]; then
    if grep -qi "mobile\|ios\|android\|react native\|flutter" .jules/pm/product-vision.md; then
        PROJECT_TYPE="$PROJECT_TYPE,MOBILE"
    fi
    
    if grep -qi "e-commerce\|shopping\|cart\|payment\|checkout\|stripe\|shopify" .jules/pm/product-vision.md; then
        PROJECT_TYPE="$PROJECT_TYPE,ECOMMERCE"
    fi
    
    if grep -qi "multi-language\|i18n\|localization\|international\|global" .jules/pm/product-vision.md; then
        PROJECT_TYPE="$PROJECT_TYPE,I18N"
    fi
    
    if grep -qi "enterprise\|multi-tenant\|saas\|b2b" .jules/pm/product-vision.md; then
        PROJECT_TYPE="$PROJECT_TYPE,ENTERPRISE"
    fi
fi

# Default to WEB if nothing detected
if [ "$PROJECT_TYPE" = "UNKNOWN" ]; then
    PROJECT_TYPE="WEB"
fi

echo "Project Type(s): $PROJECT_TYPE"
```

